documentation enrichie avec motivation et cas d''utilisation","Amélioration des performances des applications cloud avec docs-enrich-section","Compatibilité avec Toon pour la visualisation de données"],"de":["Unterstützung für Datenformate wie Avro, BSON, CVS, JSON, JSON-Schema, Message-Pack, Thrift und XML","Integration mit Scala und ZIO für Cloud-Anwendungen","Erzeugung von Dokumentation mit Motivation und Anwendungsfällen","Leistungsverbesserung von Cloud-Anwendungen mit docs-enrich-section","Kompatibilität mit Toon für Datenvisualisierung"],"pt":["Suporte a formatos de dados como avro, json e xml","Integração com linguagens de programação como scala e zio","Recursos de desempenho para aplicativos em nuvem","Exemplos de uso realistas para documentação enriquecida","Compatibilidade com message-pack e thrift"],"ru":["Поддержка форматов данных, таких как avro, json и xml","Интеграция с языками программирования, такими как scala и zio","Возможности повышения производительности для облачных приложений","Реалистичные примеры использования для обогащенной документации","Совместимость с message-pack и thrift"],"ar":["دعم صيغ البيانات مثل avro و json و xml","التكامل مع لغات البرمجة مثل scala و zio","ميزات الأداء لتطبيقات السحابة","أمثلة استخدام حقيقية لتوثيق متقدم","التوافق مع message-pack و thrift"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use docs-enrich-section","docs-enrich-section alternative","docs-enrich-section setup guide","what is docs-enrich-section","docs-enrich-section vs Thrift","docs-enrich-section JSON schema support","docs-enrich-section installation"],"zh":["docs-enrich-section","AI技能","技术文档","云原生应用","Avro","BSON","JSON","Scala","ZIO","性能优化"],"ja":["docs-enrich-section","AIエージェント","ドキュメント","クラウドネイティブアプリケーション","Avro","BSON","JSON","Scala","ZIO","パフォーマンスの最適化"],"ko":["docs-enrich-section","AI 에이전트","기술 문서","클라우드 네이티브 애플리케이션","Avro","BSON","JSON","Scala","ZIO","성능 최적화"],"es":["docs-enrich-section","aplicaciones cloud-natives","documentación enriquecida","motivación y casos de uso","formatos de datos","Scala","ZIO","Toon","rendimiento de aplicaciones cloud","herramientas de desarrollo de aplicaciones cloud"],"fr":["docs-enrich-section","applications cloud natives","documentation enrichie","motivation et cas d''utilisation","formats de données","Scala","ZIO","Toon","performances des applications cloud","outils de développement d''applications cloud"],"de":["docs-enrich-section","Cloud-Anwendungen","Dokumentation mit Motivation und Anwendungsfällen","Datenformate","Scala","ZIO","Toon","Leistung von Cloud-Anwendungen","Entwicklungstools für Cloud-Anwendungen","AI-Tools","Cloud-Computing"],"pt":["docs-enrich-section","aplicativos em nuvem","documentação enriquecida","avro","json","scala","zio","desempenho","message-pack","thrift"],"ru":["docs-enrich-section","облачные приложения","обогащенная документация","ИИ Агенты","avro","json","scala","zio","производительность","message-pack","thrift"],"ar":["docs-enrich-section","تطبيقات السحابة","توثيق متقدم","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي","avro","json","scala","zio","الأداء","message-pack","thrift"]}},"owner":"zio","repo":"zio-blocks","repoPath":"zio/zio-blocks","stars":99,"forks":136,"updatedAt":"2026-03-06T20:58:55Z","topics":["avro","bson","cvs","json","json-schema","message-pack","performance","scala","thrift","toon","xml","zio"],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"docs-enrich-section","description":"Use when a documentation section exists but lacks motivation or use-cases — thin sections that show a signature and a toy example but never explain why a reader would choose this API over alternatives.","bodyPreview":"# Enrich a Documentation Section with Motivation and Use-Cases\n\n## Overview\n\nA thin section answers *what* but not *why*. Readers landing on such a section cannot judge when\nto use the API or how it fits into the larger picture. This skill turns a thin section into one\nthat answers: what does this return, why does it exist, when is it the right choice, and what does\na realistic use look like.\n\n## Signals That a Section Needs Enriching\n\n- Shows only a signature + a trivial example (toy type, no r","body":"# Enrich a Documentation Section with Motivation and Use-Cases\n\n## Overview\n\nA thin section answers *what* but not *why*. Readers landing on such a section cannot judge when\nto use the API or how it fits into the larger picture. This skill turns a thin section into one\nthat answers: what does this return, why does it exist, when is it the right choice, and what does\na realistic use look like.\n\n## Signals That a Section Needs Enriching\n\n- Shows only a signature + a trivial example (toy type, no realistic scenario)\n- No mention of alternatives or when *not* to use this API\n- A reader could not decide between this and the nearest related operation from the section alone\n- Opening sentence restates the method name without adding context\n\n## Source Research (Do This First)\n\nBefore writing a word of prose, read the implementation:\n\n1. **Read the source** — understand what the method actually does, not just its signature\n2. **Find the contrast** — locate the nearest alternative (e.g. `rebind` vs `toSchema`) and\n   understand the exact difference in return type, requirements, and guarantees\n3. **Find real usage** — search the docs and example files for existing uses of this API to\n   anchor your realistic example\n4. **Identify the gap** — ask: \"In what situation would a reader need this but *not* the\n   alternative?\" That gap is the motivation.\n\n## The Five-Part Expansion Pattern\n\nReplace the thin section with these five parts, in order:\n\n### 1. Opening sentence\nState what the method returns and the one-line rule for when to use it. Lead with the return type\nand the key constraint that distinguishes it from alternatives.\n\n> `DynamicSchema#toSchema` returns a `Schema[DynamicValue]` — it stays fully in the dynamic world\n> and requires no bindings. Use it when you have received a `DynamicSchema` over the wire and need\n> a codec-compatible schema that enforces structural conformance without binding any Scala types.\n\n### 2. Motivation paragraph\nExplain the gap the method fills. Name the scenario where the alternative fails or is\nimpractical. Name the concrete contexts (middleware, gateways, converters, validators) where\nthis method is the right tool.\n\n### 3. Contrast sentence or table\nState explicitly: \"Use X when … Use Y instead when …\". One sentence is enough if the distinction\nis clear; a two-row table if the dimensions are multiple.\n\n| Situation | Right choice |\n|---|---|\n| No Scala types available; need structural validation only | `toSchema` |\n| Have a `BindingResolver`; need a fully operational `Schema[A]` | `rebind[A]` |\n\n### 4. Signature block\nKeep the existing signature block unchanged. Precede it with a bridging sentence ending in `:`.\n\n### 5. Realistic example\nReplace any toy example (single-field type, no context) with a scenario that could exist in a\nreal application. The scenario should exercise the method''s distinguishing behavior — the part\nthat makes it different from the alternative.\n\nChecklist for the example:\n- [ ] Models a plausible real scenario (gateway, registry, pipeline, validator)\n- [ ] Uses `mdoc:compile-only`\n- [ ] Imports everything it needs\n- [ ] No hardcoded output comments (`// None`, `// \"hello\"`, etc.)\n- [ ] Preceded by a prose sentence ending in `:`\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| Motivation paragraph is abstract (\"useful in many cases\") | Name one concrete scenario. Abstract motivation helps nobody. |\n| Contrast buried at the end | Put it before the signature block, after motivation |\n| Example uses the same toy type as before | Create a new type that reflects the motivated use-case |\n| Prose sentence before code does not end with `:` | Every sentence immediately before a code fence must end with `:` |\n| Added output comments to show what expressions return | Delete them — mdoc evaluates and renders output automatically |\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter enriching the section, run the mdoc compilation check to ensure all code examples are syntactically correct and type-check:\n\n```bash\nsbt docs/mdoc\n```\n\n**Success criterion:** The output contains **zero `[error]` lines**. Warnings are acceptable.\n\n**If mdoc reports errors:** Fix them immediately before marking the enrichment as complete. Do not commit or claim the work is done until all errors are resolved.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-07T01:50:07.493Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Technical Writing Agents needing to enhance API documentation with motivational content and practical use-cases.","zh":"适合需要使用激励内容和实用用例来增强API文档的技术写作代理。","ja":"APIドキュメントをモチベーショナルなコンテンツや実用的なユースケースで強化する必要があるテクニカルライティングエージェントに適しています。","ko":"API 문서를 동기 부여 콘텐츠와 실제 사용 사례로 강화해야 하는 기술 작성 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Escritura Técnica que necesitan mejorar la documentación de API con contenido motivacional y casos de uso prácticos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de rédaction technique ayant besoin d''améliorer la documentation de l''API avec du contenu motivant et des cas d''utilisation pratiques.","de":"Ideal für technische Schreibagenten, die die API-Dokumentation mit motivierendem Inhalt und praktischen Anwendungsfällen verbessern müssen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Redação Técnica que precisam melhorar a documentação da API com conteúdo motivacional e casos de uso práticos.","ru":"Идеально для агентов технической писанины, которым необходимо улучшить документацию API с помощью мотивационного контента и практических случаев использования.","ar":"مثالي لوسائل كتابة تقنية تحتاج إلى تعزيز توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات مع المحتوى التحفيزي والحالات العملية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform thin documentation sections into comprehensive guides, including motivation, use-cases, and realistic examples, utilizing API signatures and trivial examples to provide context.","zh":"赋予代理能力，将薄弱的文档部分转化为全面指南，包括动机、用例和真实例子，利用API签名和琐碎例子提供上下文。","ja":"エージェントに、薄いドキュメントのセクションを、動機、ユースケース、リアルな例などを含む包括的なガイドに変換する力を与え、APIのシグネチャやトリビアルな例子を使用してコンテキストを提供する。","ko":"에이전트가 동기를 부여하는 콘텐츠, 유즈 케이스 및 실제 예제를 포함하여 전체 가이드로 바뀌는 얇은 문서 섹션을 변환하여 API 서명 및 사소한 예제를 사용하여 컨텍스트를 제공하는 기능을 부여합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes transformar secciones de documentación delgadas en guías completas, incluyendo motivación, casos de uso y ejemplos realistas, utilizando firmas de API y ejemplos triviales para proporcionar contexto.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer des sections de documentation minces en guides complets, comprenant la motivation, les cas d''utilisation et les exemples réalistes, en utilisant les signatures d''API et les exemples triviaux pour fournir un contexte.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, dünne Dokumentationsabschnitte in umfassende Anleitungen umzuwandeln, einschließlich Motivation, Anwendungsfällen und realistischen Beispielen, unter Verwendung von API-Signaturen und trivialen Beispielen, um Kontext zu liefern.","pt":"Permite que os agentes transformem seções de documentação finas em guias abrangentes, incluindo motivação, casos de uso e exemplos realistas, utilizando assinaturas da API e exemplos triviais para fornecer contexto.","ru":"Позволяет агентам преобразовать тонкие разделы документации в полные руководства, включая мотивацию, случаи использования и реалистичные примеры, используя подписи API и тривиальные примеры для предоставления контекста.","ar":"تمكن الوسائل من تحويل أقسام توثيق رقيقة إلى أدلة شاملة ، بما في ذلك الدافع والحالات العملية والأمثلة الواقعية ، باستخدام التوقيعات واجهة برمجة التطبيقات والأمثلة التривيلية لتوفير السياق."},"useCases":{"en":["Enriching API documentation with motivational content","Generating realistic use-cases for API endpoints","Transforming thin documentation sections into comprehensive guides"],"zh":["用激励内容丰富API文档","为API端点生成真实的用例","将薄弱的文档部分转化为全面指南"],"ja":["APIドキュメントをモチベーショナルなコンテンツで豊富にする","APIエンドポイントのためのリアルなユースケースを生成する","薄いドキュメントのセクションを包括的なガイドに変換する"],"ko":["API 문서를 동기 부여 콘텐츠로 풍부하게 만드는 것","API 엔드ポイント에 대한 실제 유즈 케이스를 생성하는 것","얇은 문서 섹션을 포괄적인 가이드로 변환하는 것"],"es":["Enriquecer la documentación de API con contenido motivacional","Generar casos de uso realistas para puntos de conexión de API","Transformar secciones de documentación delgadas en guías completas"],"fr":["Enrichir la documentation de l''API avec du contenu motivant","Générer des cas d''utilisation réalistes pour les points de terminaison de l''API","Transformer des sections de documentation minces en guides complets"],"de":["API-Dokumentation mit motivierendem Inhalt anreichern","Erzeugen realistischer Anwendungsfälle für API-Endpunkte","Dünne Dokumentationsabschnitte in umfassende Anleitungen umwandeln"],"pt":[" Enriquecendo a documentação da API com conteúdo motivacional","Gerando casos de uso realistas para pontos de extremidade da API","Transformando seções de documentação finas em guias abrangentes"],"ru":["Обогащение документации API мотивационным контентом","Генерация реалистичных случаев использования для точек окончания API","Преобразование тонких разделов документации в полные руководства"],"ar":["تحسين توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات مع المحتوى التحفيزي","توليد حالات استخدام واقعية لنقاط نهاية واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","تحويل أقسام توثيق رقيقة إلى أدلة شاملة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to API documentation","Limited to API documentation enrichment"],"zh":["需要访问API文档","仅限于API文档的增强"],"ja":["APIドキュメントへのアクセスが必要","APIドキュメントの強化のみに限定される"],"ko":["API 문서에 접근할 수 있어야 함","API 문서 강화에만 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la documentación de API","Limitado a la mejora de la documentación de API"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à la documentation de l''API","Limité à l''enrichissement de la documentation de l''API"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die API-Dokumentation","Begrenzt auf die Anreicherung der API-Dokumentation"],"pt":["Requer acesso à documentação da API","Limitado ao enriquecimento da documentação da API"],"ru":["Требует до