e Code","Codex","pi CLIエージェント"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 플러그인 개발","plugins-guide","패널 개발","CLI 패키징","WebSocket","바이너리 엔드포인트","크로스 플랫폼 동작","Claude Code","Codex","pi CLI 에이전트"],"es":["desarrollo de plugins para agentes de inteligencia artificial","guias de configuración de plugins","mejores prácticas para plugins de agentes de inteligencia artificial","panel chrome para agentes de inteligencia artificial","operaciones y endpoints binarios para plugins","compatibilidad con plugins personalizados","exportación de plugins como habilidades con CLIs","agentes de inteligencia artificial con interfaz de texto y voz"],"fr":["développement de plugins pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle","guides d''installation de plugins","bonnes pratiques pour les plugins d''agents d''intelligence artificielle","chrome de panneau pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle","opérations et points de terminaison binaires pour les plugins","compatibilité avec des plugins personnalisés","exportation de plugins en tant que compétences avec des CLIs","agents d''intelligence artificielle avec interface texte et voix"],"de":["Entwicklung von Plug-ins für KI-Agents","Einrichtungsleitfäden für Plug-ins","Beste Praktiken für Plug-ins von KI-Agents","Panel-Chrome für KI-Agents","Operationen und binäre Endpunkte für Plug-ins","Kompatibilität mit benutzerdefinierten Plug-ins","Export von Plug-ins als Fähigkeiten mit CLIs","KI-Agents mit Text- und Sprachinterface"],"pt":["ferramentas de IA","plugins personalizados","Claude Code","Codex","pi CLI","painéis de plugins","interface de texto e voz","desenvolvimento de plugins"],"ru":["ИИ Агенты","пользовательские плагины","Claude Code","Codex","pi CLI","панели плагинов","текстовый и голосовой интерфейс","разработка плагинов"],"ar":["العاملات الذكية","ملحقات مخصصة","Claude Code","Codex","pi CLI","لوحات الملحقات","واجهة نصية وصوتية","تطوير الملحقات"]}},"owner":"kcosr","repo":"assistant","repoPath":"kcosr/assistant","stars":22,"forks":2,"updatedAt":"2026-02-22T06:37:46Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"plugins-guide","description":"Best practices for working with plugins in the kcosr/assistant repository.","bodyPreview":"# Plugin Development Guide (General Best Practices)\n\nThis guide captures reusable patterns for building panel plugins: panel chrome, operations vs. WebSocket usage, binary endpoints, icons, CLI packaging, and cross‑platform behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Panel Header Chrome (Standard Controls)\n\n**All panels should render the standard chrome header** and let the shared `PanelChromeController` wire up controls. The header is built from three sections:\n\n1. **Main** (title + optional instance dropdown)\n2. **","body":"# Plugin Development Guide (General Best Practices)\n\nThis guide captures reusable patterns for building panel plugins: panel chrome, operations vs. WebSocket usage, binary endpoints, icons, CLI packaging, and cross‑platform behavior.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Panel Header Chrome (Standard Controls)\n\n**All panels should render the standard chrome header** and let the shared `PanelChromeController` wire up controls. The header is built from three sections:\n\n1. **Main** (title + optional instance dropdown)\n2. **Plugin controls** (custom buttons)\n3. **Frame controls** (toggle/move/reorder/menu/close)\n\n### Required structure\n\n```html\n<div class=\"panel-header panel-chrome-row\" data-role=\"chrome-row\">\n  <div class=\"panel-header-main\">\n    <span class=\"panel-header-label\" data-role=\"chrome-title\">Panel Title</span>\n    <div class=\"panel-chrome-instance\" data-role=\"instance-actions\">\n      <!-- Instance dropdown markup here -->\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"panel-chrome-plugin-controls\" data-role=\"chrome-plugin-controls\">\n    <!-- plugin-specific buttons go here -->\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"panel-chrome-frame-controls\" data-role=\"chrome-controls\">\n    <!-- standard move/reorder/menu/close buttons -->\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Frame controls markup\n\nCopy the structure from existing panels like **notes** or **scheduled-sessions** (includes toggle, move, reorder, menu, close). The `PanelChromeController` attaches handlers based on `data-action` attributes.\n\n---\n\n## 2. PanelChromeController Responsibilities\n\nThe controller:\n- wires up frame controls\n- manages responsive layout\n- optionally wires up the instance dropdown\n\nYou must pass the instance dropdown container with:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"panel-chrome-instance-dropdown\" data-role=\"instance-dropdown-container\">…</div>\n```\n\nThen initialize:\n\n```ts\nchromeController = new PanelChromeController({\n  root: container,\n  host,\n  title: ''Panel Title'',\n  onInstanceChange: (instanceId) => {\n    selectedInstanceId = instanceId;\n    persistState();\n    void refreshList();\n  },\n});\n```\n\n### Multi‑profile selection (shared profiles)\n\nInstance IDs now map to **shared profiles** declared at the top level `profiles` config.\nWhen you want multi‑profile selection in a panel, opt into it explicitly:\n\n```ts\nchromeController = new PanelChromeController({\n  root: container,\n  host,\n  title: ''Notes'',\n  instanceSelectionMode: ''multi'',\n  onInstanceChange: (instanceIds) => {\n    selectedInstanceIds = instanceIds;\n    activeInstanceId = instanceIds[0] ?? ''default'';\n    persistState();\n    void refreshList();\n  },\n});\n\nchromeController.setInstances(instances, selectedInstanceIds);\n```\n\n**Context:** include both the active instance and the full selection:\n\n```ts\nhost.setContext(contextKey, {\n  instance_id: activeInstanceId,\n  instance_ids: selectedInstanceIds,\n  contextAttributes: {\n    ''instance-id'': activeInstanceId,\n    ''instance-ids'': selectedInstanceIds.join('',''),\n  },\n});\n```\n\nNotes:\n- `default` is always available (implicit).\n- Non‑default instance ids must match a configured profile id.\n- Items still belong to a single instance/profile (edits happen in one profile).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Icons and Header Dock\n\nPanel icons shown in the **header dock** come from the **panel manifest**. The manifest `icon` value must match a key in `packages/web-client/src/utils/icons.ts`.\n\nExample:\n\n```json\n\"icon\": \"fileText\"\n```\n\nIf the icon name is invalid, the UI falls back to `panelGrid` (window/grid icon).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Operations vs WebSocket for CRUD\n\n### Recommended pattern\n\nUse **HTTP operations** for CRUD and **WebSocket events only for broadcast updates**:\n\n- `list`, `create`, `update`, `delete` → **HTTP operations**\n- real‑time updates → **WebSocket `panel_update`**\n\nThis avoids startup races when WebSocket isn’t ready yet (common on mobile).\n\n### Generic helper\n\n```ts\nasync function callOperation<T>(operation: string, body: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<T> {\n  const response = await apiFetch(`/api/plugins/<pluginId>/operations/${operation}`, {\n    method: ''POST'',\n    headers: { ''content-type'': ''application/json'' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  const payload = (await response.json()) as { ok: true; result: T } | { error: string };\n  if (!response.ok || ''error'' in payload) throw new Error(payload.error);\n  return payload.result;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Extra HTTP Routes for Binary Files\n\nOperations always return JSON. For binary endpoints (file download/preview), use **`extraHttpRoutes`** in the plugin module:\n\n```ts\nextraHttpRoutes: [\n  async (_context, req, res, url, segments) => {\n    if (req.method === ''GET'' && segments[3] === ''files'') {\n      res.setHeader(''Content-Disposition'', ''inline; filename=\"...\"'');\n      res.end(fileBuffer);\n      return true;\n    }\n    return false;\n  },\n]\n```\n\nThis is documented in `docs/PLUGIN_SDK.md`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. View vs Download Behavior\n\nWhen serving files, support both:\n\n- **View (inline)** — default\n- **Download (attachment)** — via query param (e.g. `?download=1`)\n\nThis enables an “open in browser” action and a “download” action with the same endpoint.\n\n---\n\n## 7. API Base URL\n\nWhen building URLs for fetch/open, use helpers in `web-client/src/utils/api.ts`:\n\n- `apiFetch()` for relative API calls\n- `getApiBaseUrl()` for full URLs when opening externally\n\nThis ensures URLs work in **Tauri**, **Capacitor**, and **web**.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Platform-Specific Open/Save\n\n### Web\n- `window.open(url, ''_blank'')` for view\n- `<a download>` for download\n\n### Tauri Desktop\n- **View:** `plugin:shell|open`\n- **Download:** native save dialog + backend command to write file\n\n### Capacitor Mobile\n- **View:** `@capacitor/browser`\n- **Download:** `@capacitor/filesystem` + optional `@capacitor/share`\n\n---\n\n## 9. Custom CLI Bundling\n\nPlugins can ship a custom CLI by placing `bin/cli.ts` in the plugin directory.\n\nBuild system compiles this file instead of auto‑generating a CLI from operations. Use this for:\n- reading files (`--file`)\n- custom args / processing\n- client-side behaviors before calling the API\n\n---\n\n## 9.1 Skill Bundle Export Controls\n\nBy default, `npm run build:plugins` exports skills to `dist/skills/<pluginId>/`.\nTo opt out for a specific plugin, set:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skills\": { \"autoExport\": false }\n}\n```\n\nPassing `--skills <pluginId>` still forces export for that plugin.\n\nGenerated `SKILL.md` frontmatter includes `metadata.author` and `metadata.version`,\npopulated from the root `package.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Theme Variables\n\nUse shared theme variables:\n\n- `--color-text-primary`\n- `--color-text-secondary`\n- `--color-bg-hover`\n- `--color-bg-active`\n\nAvoid custom fallbacks like `--text-primary` or `prefers-color-scheme` blocks.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Shared Dialog Styling Duplication\n\nSome dialogs are rendered by shared web-client controllers but styled in multiple plugin bundles.\nFor example, list metadata dialog styles live in both:\n- `packages/plugins/official/lists/web/styles.css`\n- `packages/plugins/official/notes/web/styles.css`\n\nWhen adjusting `.list-metadata-*` rules (or similar shared dialog styles), update both files to keep\nLists and Notes consistent.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Panel Context for Chat Input\n\nPanels can provide context that is injected into user chat messages and shown in the\ncontext preview above the input. Use the panel context key and include selection data.\n\n### Required pattern\n\n```ts\nconst contextKey = getPanelContextKey(host.panelId());\nhost.setContext(contextKey, {\n  type: ''list'', // or ''artifacts'', ''note'', etc.\n  id: activeContainerId,\n  name: activeContainerName,\n  description: activeContainerDescription ?? '''',\n  selectedItemIds,\n  selectedItems, // [{ id, title }]\n  selectedItemCount: selectedItemIds.length,\n  contextAttributes: {\n    ''instance-id'': selectedInstanceId,\n    // add custom attributes like ''selected-text'' for text selections\n  },\n});\nservices.notifyContextAvailabilityChange();\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `type`, `id`, and `name` are used to build the `<context ... />` line in chat.\n- `selectedItemIds`/`selectedItems` populate selection context (e.g., list rows).\n- `contextAttributes` is a key/value bag for extra metadata (keys should be kebab-case).\n- Call `services.notifyContextAvailabilityChange()` after updates so the preview refreshes.\n- Listen for `assistant:clear-context-selection` if you support selection clearing.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Recommended Panel Lifecycle\n\nOn mount:\n- fetch instances via HTTP\n- fetch initial list via HTTP\n- subscribe to WebSocket updates\n\nOn visibility change:\n- refresh list via HTTP\n\n---\n\nThis guide is meant as a reusable checklist for future plugin work (operations + binary endpoints, panel chrome, icons, CLI, and cross‑platform behaviors).\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T06:41:04.657Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Developer Agents needing customizable productivity workflows with plugin architecture support for Claude Code, Codex, and pi CLI agents.","zh":"非常适合需要可定制的生产力工作流和插件架构支持的Claude Code、Codex和pi CLI代理的开发者代理。","ja":"Claude Code、Codex、pi CLIエージェントをサポートするカスタマイズ可能な生産性ワークフローとプラグインアーキテクチャを必要とする開発者エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Claude Code, Codex, pi CLI 에이전트를 지원하는 맞춤형 생산성 워크플로 및 플러그인 아키텍처가 필요한 개발자 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Desarrollador que necesitan flujos de trabajo de productividad personalizables con soporte de arquitectura de plugins para Claude Code, Codex y agentes de línea de comandos pi.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Développeur ayant besoin de flux de travail de productivité personnalisables avec une prise en charge de l''architecture de plugins pour Claude Code, Codex et les agents CLI pi.","de":"Perfekt für Entwickler-Agenten, die benutzerdefinierte Produktivitäts-Workflows mit Plugin-Architektur-Unterstützung für Claude Code, Codex und pi-CLI-Agenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Desenvolvedores que necessitam de fluxos de trabalho de produtividade personalizáveis com suporte a arquitetura de plugins para Claude Code, Codex e agentes pi CLI.","ru":"Идеально для агентов-разработчиков, которым требуются настраиваемые рабочие процессы производительности с поддержкой архитектуры плагинов для Claude Code, Codex и агентов pi CLI.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المطورين الذين يحتاجون إلى سلاسل عمل إنتاجية قابلة للتخصيص مع دعم هندسة البرامج الإضافية لـ Claude Code و Codex ووكلاء pi CLI."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to extend workflows with custom plugins using WebSocket usage, binary endpoints, and CLI packaging, while ensuring cross-platform behavior and standard panel chrome headers.","zh":"赋予代理扩展工作流的能力，使用WebSocket、二进制端点和CLI打包，并确保跨平台行为和标准面板Chrome头部。","ja":"WebSocket、バイナリエンドポイント、CLIパッケージを使用してワークフローを拡張し、クロスプラットフォーム動作と標準パネルChromeヘッダーを保証するエージェントを可能にします。","ko":"WebSocket, 바이너리 엔드포인트 및 CLI 패키지를 사용하여 워크플ロー 확장 및 크로스 플랫폼 동작 및 표준 패널 크롬 헤더 보장을 가능하게 하는 에이전트입니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a extender flujos de trabajo con plugins personalizados utilizando el uso de WebSocket, puntos de conexión binarios y empaquetado de CLI, garantizando al mismo tiempo un comportamiento entre plataformas y encabezados de panel estándar.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''étendre les flux de travail avec des plugins personnalisés en utilisant l''utilisation de WebSocket, des points de terminaison binaires et l''emballage CLI, tout en garantissant un comportement cross-plateforme et des en-têtes de panneau standard.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Workflows mit benutzerdefinierten Plugins zu erweitern, indem sie die Verwendung von WebSocket, binären Endpunkten und CLI-Verpackung nutzen, während sie gleichzeitig ein plattformübergreifendes Verhalten und Standard-Panel-Headern sicherstellen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a estender fluxos de trabalho com plugins personalizados usando utilização de WebSocket, endpoints binários e embalagem de CLI, garantindo comportamento entre plataformas e cabeçalhos de painel padrão.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью расширять рабочие процессы с помощью пользовательских плагинов, используя WebSocket, бинарные конечные точки и упаковку CLI, обеспечивая поведение на разных платформах и стандартные заголовки панели.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من توسيع سلاسل العمل باستخدام البرامج الإضافية المخصصة باستخدام استخدام WebSocket ونقاط النهاية الثنائية وتعبئة CLI ، مع ضمان السلوك عبر المنصات وروابط لوحة القيادة القياسية."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing custom plugins for panel-based personal assistants","Integrating WebSocket usage for real-time workflow updates","Creating cross-platform compatible plugins for various agents"],"zh":["为基于面板的个人助手开发自定义插件","集成WebSocket以实现实时工作流更新","为各种代理创建跨平台兼容的插件"],"ja":["パネルベースのパーソナルアシスタント用のカスタムプラグインを開発する","WebSocketを統合してリアルタイムのワークフロー更新を実現する","さまざまなエージェント用のクロスプラットフォーム互換性のあるプラグインを作成する"],"ko":["패널 기반 개인 어시스턴트를 위한 맞춤형 플러그인 개발","실시간 워크플ロー 업데이트를 위해 WebSocket 통합","다양한 에이전트를 위한 크로스 플랫폼 호환 플러그인 생성"],"es":["Desarrollar plugins personalizados para asistentes personales basados en paneles","Integrar el uso de WebSocket para actualizaciones de flujo de trabajo en tiempo real","Crear plugins compatibles con varias plataformas para diferentes agentes"],"fr":["Développer des plugins personnalisés pour les assistants personnels basés sur les panneaux","Intégrer l''utilisation de WebSocket pour des mises à jour de flux de travail en temps réel","Créer des plugins compatibles avec plusieurs plateformes pour différents agents"],"de":["Entwicklung benutzerdefinierter Plugins für panelbasierte persönliche Assistenten","Integrieren der WebSocket-Verwendung für Echtzeit-Workflow-Updates","Erstellung plattformübergreifender Plugins für verschiedene Agenten"],"pt":["Desenvolver plugins personalizados para assistentes pessoais baseados em painel","Integrar utilização de WebSocket para atualizações de fluxo de trabalho em tempo real","Criar plugins compatíveis com várias plataformas para vários agentes"],"ru":["Разработка пользовательских плагинов для персональных помощников на основе панелей","Интеграция использования WebSocket для обновлений рабочих процессов в реальном времени","Создание плагинов, совместимых с несколькими платформами, для различных агентов"],"ar":["تنمية البرامج الإضافية المخصصة للمساعدين الشخصيين المستندة إلى اللوحة","دمج استخدام WebSocket لتحديثات سلاسل العمل في الوقت الفعلي","إنشاء البرامج الإضافية المتوافقة عبر المنصات لعدة وكلاء"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires knowledge of plugin development best practices","Limited to agents supporting Claude Code, Codex, and pi CLI"],"zh":["需要插件开发最佳实践的知识","仅限支持Claude Code、Codex和pi CLI的代理"],"ja":["プラグイン開発のベストプラクティスに関する知識が必要","Claude Code、Codex、pi CLIをサポートするエージェントのみ"],"ko":["플러그인 개발 모범 사례에 대한 지식이 필요함","Claude Code, Codex, pi CLI를 지원하는 에이전트만 해당"],"es":["Requiere conocimiento de las mejores prácticas de desarrollo de plugins","Limitado a agentes que admiten Claude Code, Codex y pi CLI"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances sur les meilleures pratiques de développement de plugins","Limité aux agents prenant en charge Claude Code, Codex et pi CLI"],"de":["Benötigt Kenntnisse über die besten Praktiken für die Plugin-Entwicklung","Begrenzt auf Agenten, die Claude Code, Codex und pi-CLI unterstützen"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento das melhores práticas de desenvolvimento de plugins","Limitado a agentes que suportam Claude Code, Codex e pi CLI"],"ru":["Требует знания лучших практик разработки плагинов","Ограничен агентами, поддерживающими Claude Code, Codex и pi CLI"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة أفضل الممارسات لتطوير البرامج الإضافية","محدود بالوكلاء الذين يدعمون Claude Code و Codex ووكلاء pi CLI"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"693e688f634c6a92ec1e2d867dd752cd2b08fab3c6453e18bef72acf14fecb94","qualityScore":47}');
